What a close call.  This is what gives nethack the addictive thrill.

spoilers follow...

My first game of reasonable length as a Barbarian.  The quest was
ok... I have to say that the villians in the two quests I've done
so far (B and S) were pretty anticlimactic.  They talked real big,
teleported around a bit, and died after a few whacks.

Well the prize was a gem called the Heart of Ahriman.  Pelias told
me to wear it for protection, but I tried 'P', 'W', and 'a', to no
avail.  I guess just having it in your possession in considered
wearing it.  I keep it outside my bag of holding, like my luckstone.

While I was working on the quest, I had to pray because cockatrices
got me -- btw why don't unicorn horns cure stoning? -- and
while Crom was limbering my limbs, he chose me to do something for
Balance and gave me the Vorpal Blade.  Pretty cool, especially now
that it's +4.  But the language makes me a little queasy --
  Vorpal Blade cuts off the water nymph's head!
  Vorpal Blade cuts off the little dog's head!  The little dog yelps!
  Vorpal Blade cuts off the Elven King's head!
That almost makes it seem like murder... I never think of killing
monsters in quite such graphic terms.

Well, I was tooling along on the first level of Gehennom, wearing
an amulet that I thought was reflection (by elimination -- the others
I'd either identified already, or eliminated because the effects should 
have been apparent).  Blindfolded, I noticed a black dragon on the other
side of the screen.  Fine, I'll be safe with my amulet of reflection,
and I'll kill him and eat him.

In the meantime I was fooling around with a nurse, trying to get a few
hit points... I got 10 or 20 total.  Finally I get near the black dragon,
and I have my blindfold on, and:
  The blast of disintegration hits you!
I observed this sentence in a state of complete calm.  Obviously I wasn't
dead, so there was nothing to worry about.  Good, the amulet worked, I
assure myself -- but why didn't it say, "It reflects off your amulet"?
Hmm.  Maybe because I had my blindfold on?
So I take it off, walk around some more and try to get the dragon to blast
me again.  He obliges.  Still the same message, no "reflect" message.
And I noticed that my hp were steadier than the Nikkei.
Quel strange!  Maybe something else -- maybe now magic resistance somehow
encompasses disintegration resistance?  So I check my armor. 
  I'm not wearing any !!  Just my +1 Hawaiian shirt !!
That was a potentially fatal stupid mistake, I tell myself.
So it must have been my amulet, right?  Well, I'm really curious now,
so I get out a scroll of identify (there are so many lying around!)
and id the amulet.  Restful sleep!!  (I had failed to figure out what
it was, apparently because my sleep resistance rendered it ineffectual.)
So what had protected me?
  Ah, must be that when Crom chose me for Balance, he granted me
disintegration resistance.  Still, why no message like "you feel a
mild buzz"?  Shrugging, I kill and eat the dragon.
   You feel very firm.
No, I didn't have disint-res before.
Could it have been Vorpal Blade protecting me?

        Finally I concluded that it must have been the Heart of Ahriman
all along.  I guess I owe my life to that gem -- how scary to think
that I owe this entire game to total oblivious dumb luck!

Phew.

Well from now on I'll be more careful.


By the way, if it was the Heart of Ahriman protecting me, shouldn't
there have been some kind of message?  A message describing what
the Heart does, or just that I feel protected or something....

